sequenceDiagram
    participant User as CLI User
    participant CLI as kubectl-odh<br/>(rhai-cli)
    participant K8s as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS
    participant OLM as OLM API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS
    participant TrustYAI as TrustYAI Service<br/>443/TCP HTTPS

    Note over User,K8s: Flow 1: CLI → Kubernetes API (diagnose, status, get, etc.)
    User->>CLI: kubectl odh diagnose<br/>kubeconfig flags
    CLI->>K8s: SelfSubjectAccessReview<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+, Bearer token
    K8s-->>CLI: AccessReview Result
    CLI->>K8s: GET /apis (resource discovery)<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    K8s-->>CLI: API Resources
    CLI->>K8s: GET /watch resources<br/>HTTPS/WSS TLS 1.2+
    K8s-->>CLI: Resource State
    CLI-->>User: Formatted Output (table/JSON)

    Note over User,TrustYAI: Flow 2: TrustYAI Metrics Migration
    User->>CLI: kubectl odh migrate trustyai
    CLI->>K8s: GET Route (label/name lookup)<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+, kubeconfig creds
    K8s-->>CLI: TrustYAI Route URL
    CLI->>TrustYAI: GET /metrics (backup)<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+ (InsecureSkipVerify)<br/>Bearer token from kubeconfig
    TrustYAI-->>CLI: Metrics Data
    CLI->>TrustYAI: POST /metrics (restore)<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+ (InsecureSkipVerify)<br/>Bearer token from kubeconfig
    TrustYAI-->>CLI: Restore Confirmation
    CLI-->>User: Migration Result

    Note over User,K8s: Flow 3: MCP Server (optional, AI agent integration)
    participant Agent as MCP Client<br/>(AI Agent)
    Agent->>CLI: JSON-RPC tool call<br/>SSE 8080/TCP or stdio
    CLI->>K8s: Kubernetes operations<br/>HTTPS TLS 1.2+, kubeconfig creds
    K8s-->>CLI: API Response
    CLI-->>Agent: JSON-RPC result
